3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3\n3 3 3 3 3 3\nwhere the pair's output is\n2 3 3 3 3 4\n2 3 9 3 3 3\n3 3 9 3 2 2\n4 3 9 3 3 3\n3 3 9 9 9 3\nFailed checks in this instance: 1 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    # The repeated 3x3 background is a lattice. Its colored intersections\n    # form pairs of identical cells; collapse each horizontal pair and\n    # translate lattice coordinates into the compact output canvas.\n    h, w = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    rr = list(range(2, h, 3))\n    cc = list(range(1, w, 3))\n    marks = [[grid[r][c] for c in cc] for r in rr]\n\n    # Pair columns in the lattice and map them to output columns.\n    # The empty lattice gap between pairs is retained as an output blank.\n    out = [[3] * 6 for _ in range(5)]\n    pair_to_col = {0: 0, 3: 2, 5: 4, 7: 5}\n    for y in range(min(5, len(marks))):\n        for start, x in pair_to_col.items():\n            vals = marks[y][start:start + 2]\n            color = next((v for v in vals if v not in (1, 3, 8)), None)\n            if color is not None:\n                out[y][x] = color\n    return out\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[9,9,1,1,1,1],[9,9,1,1,1,1],[9,9,9,9,7,7],[9,9,9,9,7,7],[9,9,4,4,7,7],[2,2,4,4,2,2],[2,2,4,4,2,2]]}},{"step":156,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1792558302.633,"t1":1792558310.493,"alias":"task-f15c46e2","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n2 3 3 3 3 4\n2 3 9 3 3 4\n2 3 9 3 3 2\n4 3 9 3 3 2\n4 3 9 3 3 3\nwhere the pair's output is\n2 3 3 3 3 4\n2 3 9 3 3 3\n3 3 9 3 2 2\n4 3 9 3 3 3\n3 3 9 9 9 3\nFailed checks in this instance: 2 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"{\"action\":\"request_demos\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"demo"}},{"step":156,"kind":"obs